## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical CV pipeline using lightweight, non-ML methods for a common task.

## Key Concepts
- Circle detection with Hough transform
- Radius-based grouping for coin types
- Noise/shadow handling with blur and histogram equalization
- Validation with synthetic data

## Code Example
```javascript
// OpenCV.js-like pseudocode
let src = cv.imread('table.jpg');
cv.cvtColor(src, src, cv.COLOR_RGBA2GRAY);
cv.equalizeHist(src, src);
cv.GaussianBlur(src, new cv.Size(9,9), 2);
let circles = new cv.Mat();
cv.HoughCircles(src, circles, cv.HOUGH_GRADIENT, 1.2, 20, 50, 30, 10, 60);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you address perspective distortions?
- How would you validate robustness with lighting changes?

## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests end-to-end 3D understanding of dense retail shelves and edge adaptation for unseen products.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose with template-based fit
- Synthetic+real data strategy for crowded shelves
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with lightweight adapters
- Occlusion-aware pose and neighbor interaction modeling

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(input) {
  const features = backbone(input);
  const detections = detectorHead(features);
  const poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  return {detections, poses};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How do you handle multiple identical items and permutation ambiguity?
- How would you evaluate robustness to lighting and glare on glossy shelves?
